{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-24T07:04:53.631Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e22e962c57db3775644e8f9e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1571\n\nIntake only: reporter reproduction below has not yet been independently run against main. The item remains open and unclaimed. This report arrived after PR #1570 merged and is distinct from its flag-default discovery fixes.\n\n## Summary\n\nFields registered by an extension through `registerItemFields` are persisted and returned by full reads, but `get`/`list`/`search` field projection refuses them as unknown. An agent that needs one custom value must make a refused call and then a full read, which pulls the whole item into context.\n\n## Reproduction (pm 2026.10.24, plain directory, no git)\n\n```ts\nimport { PmClient } from '@unbrained/pm-cli';\nimport { mkdir, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { resolve } from 'node:path';\nconst cwd = resolve('custom-repro'); const ext = resolve('custom-repro/ext');\nawait mkdir(ext, { recursive: true });\nawait writeFile(ext + '/package.json', JSON.stringify({ name: 'probe-field', version: '0.1.0', type: 'module' }));\nawait writeFile(ext + '/manifest.json', JSON.stringify({ name: 'probe-field', version: '0.1.0', manifest_version: 2, entry: './index.ts', capabilities: ['schema'] }));\nawait writeFile(ext + '/index.ts', `import {defineExtension} from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/authoring';\nexport default defineExtension({activate(api){api.registerItemFields([{name:'probe_score',type:'number',optional:true}]);}});`);\nconst c = new PmClient({ cwd, pmRoot: cwd + '/.agents/pm', author: 'probe' });\nawait c.init(undefined, { defaults: true, agentGuidance: 'skip' });\nawait c.packageInstall(ext);\nconst id = (await c.create({ type: 'Task', title: 'Probe', field: ['probe_score=3'] })).item.id;\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(await c.get(id, { full: true })).includes('\"probe_score\":3')); // true\nawait c.get(id, { fields: 'id,probe_score' }); // throws\n```\n\n## Observed\n\n- The full read contains `probe_score: 3`.\n- `get(id, { fields: 'id,probe_score' })` throws `PmCliError: Unknown get --fields value(s): probe_score`. The CLI form (`pm get <id> --fields id,probe_score`) and projected `list`/`search` refuse the same way (`unknown_field_projection`, exit 2).\n- The suggested recovery drops the requested field. The retried query is valid but cannot answer the question.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe set of projectable fields includes the active runtime custom-field registry, the same way in the SDK and the CLI, and keeps the key, type and value. If projecting custom fields is deliberately unsupported, the refusal should say so and point to a read that actually returns the value.\n\n## Cost\n\nRecovering one numeric field takes two calls and about 6.5 KB of output (a 5.1 KB refusal plus a 1.4 KB full read), about 1,600 tokens. Projected `list` and `search` refusals are 4.7 KB and 6.2 KB. Any package that stores typed data in custom fields (pm-rl scores, pm-jev decisions, pm-evidence fingerprints) forces full reads into agent context.\n\n## Duplicate check\n\nSearched `registerItemFields`, `custom field projection`, `unknown_field_projection` and `fields custom registered` (all states). #97 and #839 (setting and typing custom fields) are fixed. #156, #1364 and #1386 cover context depth and projection recovery for built-in fields, not runtime-registered ones."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1571"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1571: allow projection of active extension item fields across read surfaces"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Reported on published 2026.10.24: full reads retain typed registerItemFields values but get/list/search --fields reject them as unknown_field_projection. Preserve extension-defined context through compact SDK and CLI reads using the active runtime field registry. Intake only; independently reproducing and implementing the fix are future work."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["extensions","github","projection","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-24T07:04:53.631Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-24T07:04:53.631Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Add a sandbox reproduction against the active runtime registry covering SDK and CLI get/list/search.; Preserve numeric and other supported declared field values and reject truly unknown names without silently dropping requested fields.; Keep CLI and MCP adapters on shared SDK projection contracts and update discovery and recovery where needed.; Prove extension activation isolation and built-in projection compatibility through meaningful regression tests and linked evidence."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"Reporter: published npm CLI and SDK 2026.10.24 in a plain temporary directory without git; local schema-capability extension registers optional numeric probe_score."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Use the attached source reproduction in the item body: init a temporary tracker; activate a local registerItemFields extension; create probe_score=3; compare full get with projected SDK get and CLI get/list/search."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Active extension fields are projectable in SDK and CLI get/list/search with their original names and types. Unknown fields still produce truthful recovery that preserves caller intent."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Reporter observed probe_score=3 in a full SDK get but selecting id,probe_score is rejected by SDK get and CLI get/list/search. Recovery drops the requested field; not independently reproduced during intake."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.10.24"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"SDK read projection and extension field registry"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"Extension packages must fetch full rows to recover requested domain fields; reporter measured two calls and about 1600 tokens to read one scalar."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-cxr0jb","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-24T07:04:53.631Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-qvdj","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-24T07:04:53.631Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-24T07:04:53.631Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check: complete all-status strict export read 3093 of 3093 items with no unreadables or omissions. Searched registerItemFields and custom field projection plus the live open and in-progress lists. Closed custom-field setters and closed intent projections cover adjacent completed work; neither covers selecting active extension-defined fields. No open exact duplicate found. Intake remains open and unclaimed; this records the new GitHub report without claiming a reproduced defect or an implemented fix."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"b6bbef5f97962ebcb101245157912c3627e3805204d8b45963c88d4ef0ee14b8","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"492cf510650cea95b9c22cb57fcb803c7946f427288fb9ed6d5fc1810dc2f129"}
